`ScrollToIndexAsyncCore` doesn't re-check `token` after the render-commit rendezvous, and it doesn't pass the token through to the JS interop call. This can still perform the final scroll even if the caller cancels (or a later call supersedes it). Consider checking/throwing for cancellation before `AlignToTargetAsync`, and propagating the token into the JS interop invocation so cancellation reliably prevents viewport movement.
